(2) Agree to a dismissal, amendment, or enter a nolle prosequi on any accusation, citation, or summons filed in the municipal court as provided by law as to an indigent defendant, except that the public defender shall not have the authority to agree to a dismissal or a nolle prosequi in any case in which the indigent accused is charged with a violation of state law other than one which the municipal court has jurisdiction to try and dispose of such offense.
(3) Request and utilize the assistance of any other public defender, or other attorney employed by an agency of the state or its political subdivisions or authorities in the defense of any criminal action.
(Ord. No. 2020-05, § 1, 3-2-2020)

802:
